            <ArticleTitle>[Surgical treatment of obesity: status quo].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1383-4, 1386-8, 1390</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00108-014-3557-z</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Obesity surgery has a proven beneficial effect on mortality for patients with a body mass index (BMI) &gt;40 kg/m(2). For patients with type 2 diabetes and a BMI &gt;35 kg/m(2), obesity surgery has also shown to improve metabolic control compared to conservative therapy. Treatment should be embedded in an interdisciplinary and experienced setting. Lifelong follow-up is mandatory. Due to the complexity of the patient collective, future treatment should focus on centers with a true interdisciplinary infrastructure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
